This [[id:495f274d-80ec-47a2-93dc-733355ef9b9c][essay]] will look at the [[id:df5ce106-417e-4489-be83-5b7f35c11bd3][lineage of liberal ontology]] as a [[id:4b1d8087-3b03-47e5-b4f3-2803ff68dbc3][mode]] of [[id:02eb741c-d586-4295-8d49-e2109097d99b][kyriarchist genring]], itself a mode of [[id:f1044a93-756d-4f1f-86b2-317311d4fe38][kyriarchist worlding]]. Liberal ontology [[id:d7989cc6-3c09-4fd1-be48-55ef1f958cd5][determines]] what is through knowing. That [[id:d7649d6a-66cc-4efb-b20f-5f2b960bcab8][knowing]] is the result of [[id:b180208b-8e7d-4fcf-8b6c-20ec3b4c5a0e][naming]], an [[id:32e00173-c695-4bb6-b0d2-9dc17fec128b][act]] which [[id:ee30fde6-1d49-47fa-95a7-9b1629e897ec][stabilizes]] what *[[id:7706e59a-4dca-436b-a67c-66a45e9eca8d][is]]*, into what is [[id:f2ec0517-54e1-4cf3-ae11-ad82308bbca0][known]], into a new [[id:771ea0d8-c518-434d-b302-72f2d97045eb][unknown]]: a new being, whose whose existence  named by its [[id:40a4244e-a940-40f0-a4bb-0e6e265e96f3][relationship]] to the known, [[id:c8ba8cf5-2718-43e7-9f27-126319bdfe40][inducing]] a [[id:596666b4-45be-4850-866a-8d58f8a22fb3][recursive structure]] of [[id:33c6945f-b093-46e9-8750-5e3cfd6514dd][determination]] in which the known determines the unknown.

